  "sfx": {
    "palette": "hollow",
    "about": "The middle. Thirds drop out of the impacts: hits, shots and kills are root-and-fifth, so the mode stays ambiguous and cold. Mechanisms keep their thirds so puzzles still read as friendly.",
    "pitchRule": "tones are played in order. from \"chord\": index into the triad of the chord in force at the cue's grid line, stacked upward from the chord root in MIDI octave `octave` (C4 = 60; 0 root, 1 third, 2 fifth, 3 root an octave up ...). from \"scale\": 0-based degree of the level scale in `octave`. perTape: add the acting cassette index (0..3) to index, so four selves acting together spell the chord. \"off\" replaces \"tones\" for off / close events, \"heavy\" for power >= 6.",
    "latency": {
      "about": "OPEN-23 / MUSIC-05..07. Only the audible accent is placed, never the simulation event, and only LATE: on the next grid line at or after the event. Impact classes also fire an immediate soft transient (30% gain, first pitch) at the event itself whenever the accent is more than 12 ms away, so feedback is never mushy. Player inputs are not quantised.",
      "grid": "sixteenth of the tempo as heard (the master sixteenth, subdivided by the power of two the world is slowed by while recording at tape speed s)",
      "maxLateness": "one grid step",
      "sixteenthMs": 125,
      "impactGrid": "sixteenth",
      "impactGridMs": 125,
      "impactGridNote": "Proposal beyond the prototype: impact classes use the 32nd grid when a sixteenth is longer than 130 ms (bpm below 116), which keeps the worst-case delay of a hit under about 100 ms. All other cues stay on the sixteenth. Both grids nest inside the music.",
      "immediateTransientMinDelayMs": 12,
      "mergeRule": "same class and same grid line -> one cue (gain x1.08 per extra event, capped at 1); at most 8 cues per grid line, by priority"
    },
